        <p>NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN, that the next GENERAL QUARTER SESSIONS of the peace 1!Pl• the couNry Ol onEs [ER will be holden at the COURT HOUSE, KNUTSFORD, in and for the said on :IIoNDAy, the 15th day of October next, at Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon, when the Grand Jury bill be empannelled. , The hearing of all Appeals arising within the Hun- 'reds of Bucklow, Maccle,field, and Northwich, forming the Knutsford District, and the trials of all prisoners Committed from such Hundreds.will take place at such essions. The Grand and Petty Juries for the Knut9ford bistriet must be in attendance at the Court House, itnutsford, at the opening of the Court on MONDAY, the 15th day of October, at Eleven o'clock in the Fotenoon. THE COURT will be adjourned to the Castle of Cbester, 00 Tnuasner, the 18th day of October next, at Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon' when another Grand Jury will be empannelled• The hearing of all Appeals arising within the Hundreds of Broxton, Eddisbury. Nantwich and Wirral, forming the Chester District, and the trials of all prisoners committed from the last- Mentioned Hundreds will take place at such adjourned Sessions. The Grand and Petty Juries for the Chester bistrict must be in attendance at the Castle of Chester, at the opening of the Court on THURSDAY, the 18th day of October next, at Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon. REGINALD POTTS, Clerk of the Peace for the County of Chester. Chester, 4th September, 1900.</p>
        <p>COUNTY OF CHESTER. DISEASES OF ANIMALS ACT, 1894. FOOT-AND-MOUTTI DISEASE. No. IS HEREBY GIVEN, that at a Meeting of the Executive Committee of the Local Authority :.1,1 the County of Chester, held at the Crewe Arms hotel, on Friday, the 28th day of September. 1900, IT AS ORDERED that from and after the Bth day of 9ctober. 1900, the movement of Animals (i e., CATTLE, ANIMALS GOATS, AND ALL OTHER RUMINATING AND SWINE) into the District of the Local Authority of the County of Chester BE ABSOLUTELY a?ROHIBITED from the District of any Local Authority 'ad England or Waits or Scotland, in which the Board of 4griculture may by any Order or Orders consequent up- " an Outbreak or Outbreaks of Foot-and-mouth Disease, anstitute in whole or in part a scheduled district, or ;d which Foot and Mouth Disease exists, such prohibi- :lan to operate so long only as the Order or Orders of Board of Agriculture constituting such district or "Istricts continue in operation and to lapse on the revo- tation thereof by the Board, or on notification from the Poard that Foot-and-Mouth Disease has ceased to exist Id the District of any such Authority. ttEGINALD POTTS, Clerk to thr4 Cneshire County Council. Chester, 6th October, 1900. NOTE. The Board of Agriculture have at the date bereof pre- Ilaribed scheduled districts in whole or in part in the following Couaties, viz :—Wilts, Somerset. The District of the Local Authority ,)f the County of Chester does not include the City of Chester, nor any of the Municipal Boroughs situate therein. ,N.Animals shall not be deemed be be moved into the auistrict of the L3cal Authority of the County of Chester "am the District of any Authority in which there is holly or in part a Foot and Mouth Disease Scheduled "iatrict, or in which Foot and Mouth Disease exists, ,N'there they are moved through such district or any part hereof bylrailway without unnecessary delay,and with- di:lt the animals being uutrucked or rebooked within such district or any part thereof. Animals cannot be moved into the County of Chester ;hat may have been at any time during the continuance of !Le foregoing Regulations within the astrict of any glathorit'y in•whictt there is wholly or in part a Foot- nd-Mouth Disease Scheduled District, or in which Foot 'dcl Mouth Disease exists. Any offence against the above Regulations is deemed. -41 pffenoe against the Diseases of Animate 4.. ct, 1894, Ivhich renders the offender liable to the penalties therein Tirovided.</p>
