        <p>UNPRECEDENTED PROSPERITY AT .PIT TS' S, LONDON-ROAD, MANCHESTER (Just past Station, through Railway Arch). ALSO AT PITTS'S PANTHEON, GAYTHORN (Just past Manchester Can tral Station). BUSINESS HOURS, 8 to 7. SATURDAYS. 8 to 9. THE RENOWNED GENERAL FURNISHERS. DITTS'S STILL PURSUE THE PATH OF PRO- gress, their turnover during the Anniversary Sale j ust closed EXCEEDED BY £1,500 that of the same sale last year. Evidently the public fully appreciate the extraordinary value of Pitts's Furnishings, having implicit confidence in their excellence and reliability. PITTS'S' INSTITUTED ECONOMICAL FURNISH - lug—Before the advent of this renowned firm, over half a century ago, it was utterly impossible to purchase any- thing like a decent House of Furniture for less than two or three hundred pounds. But now, thanks to PITTS'S CELE- BRATED HOUSES OF FURNITURE at 151, 221, 281, 381. 50, 75, and 100 guineas, a very good show can be made, and a comfortable and tasteful home obtained for a comparative tritle.Year in Year out PITTS'S have advertised these Houses of Furniture as the VERY BEST VALUE OBTAINABLE, so hat at present, within fifty miles of Manchester, there is hardly a town or village that does not contain them. 'PITTS'S MAKE A POINT OF ALWAYS 1 OFFERING only such goods as can be depended upon Articles that will be a credit Lot only to their poss4isor, but also to the firm that supplied them. Whether an order be great or small, the utmost care and attention is bestowed upon it. consequently one customer after another is pleased and satisfied, and recommend PITTS'S. with the inevitable result that PITTS'S Trade grows greater and greater, P ITTS'S ARE DISTINGUISHED BY THE _1 VIGOUR and boldness of initiative—no enterprise being too great for them—the unvarying good quality and durability of their wares and the thorough soundness of their business methods. These combined i have enabled PIT fS'S to blush aside all feeble and ineffectual attempts at competition, and now PITTS'S stand in a position by them- selves, and are justly entitled to be proclaimed by Press and Public the Largest, Best, and Cheapest General Furnishers. DITT'S HAVE GAINED THE PROUD POSI- TION they occupy by dint of undeviating attentioa to the minutest details. From day to day during the last fifty- five years Furnishing problems have been constantly arising. These PITI'S have solved, and this accumulated experience PITTS'S freely offer for the benefit of their numerous customers. Then why not share in it by giving PITTS'S your order instead of placing it in the hands of incompetents who will only make a" mull "of it, whilst charging double PITTS'S prices. Purrs's NEW ILLUSTRATED FURNISHING GUIDE is universally recognised as the handsomest and most comprehensive extant. It contains 700 extremely artistic designs. each article being priced, and shows clearly HOW TO SAVE FIFTY PER CENT. Forwarded post free. Cash prices only quoted. Deferred payments by arrangement. PITTS'S BEDSTEADS and BEDDlNG.—Largest and bast selection, being cleared out at giving-away prices. Rare chance for cheap lines. Do not miss them. pITTS'S CARPETS and FLOOR COVERINGS.— .1 Grand Display. All British makes, choicest designs, many o/ which exclusively exquisitely blended colourings. Laid and Fitted Free of Charge. pPITTS'S POPULAR PIANOS,—NEW INSTRU- MENTS,I. guaranteed TEN YEARS. by Collard, Pohlman, and many other renowned makers, at considerably UNDER usual prices. SECOND-HAND INSTRUMENTS, splendid selection, from £8 to £5O Cottage Grand, some of which cost double and treble. Cash price only quoted. Deferred payments from Bs. monthly. Delivered first payment. Pianos Exchanged. Astounding saving. DITTS'S CYCLES, BASSIN E'TTES, MAIL CARTS, 1 LAMPS, CHINA. GLASS, Earthenware. Magnificent Selection. Astounding Value. Well worth inspection. PITTS'S OFFICE and LIBRARY FURNITURE. —Every Description of Bookcases, Secretaires, Desks, Stools, Chairs, Safes, Copying Presses, at about Half City